                                   "title":  "Letterboxd review of Pulse",
                                   "snippet":  "[Letterboxd Review of \"Pulse\"] I watched this as a solo double bill with \"Murder by phone\" for it\u0027s ludite nature of technophobia but this one treats it much like \"Maximum overdrive\" in which we never get to know where the curse comes from much like \"Safe\" by Todd Haynes. I have to say this is visually stunning and the audio texture is great and I love the story from a kids point of view but it is a little ridiculous to have a key lock on the inside of the house but I guess that\u0027s the films contrivance to showcase our need on security and boy do they showcase the use of electricity with imadgry but for the stories narrativ",
